WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.230
Before getting out of bed, many Jews say
a short prayer of thanks for waking up.

2
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.200
At meals there is a short
blessing before eating,

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.160
and a longer grace
after a meal with bread.

4
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:15.380
And on the doorways of a Jewish home,
a small case is fixed to the right-hand

5
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:16.570
doorpost.

6
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.850
So why do many Jews touch that small
case every time they walk into a room?

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.740
In this mission, you'll
follow a Jewish day of prayer,

8
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.840
from waking to sleeping.

9
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:31.660
Then you'll compare set prayers from a
prayer book with prayer in your own words.

10
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.830
Your mission: find out why that small
case on the doorframe matters so much.
